[Host] About seven hundred thirty people, working in seven departments.

72
00:12:20,104 --> 00:12:43,936
[Host] That's all for today. Japan launched its new National Intelligence Bureau on July thirty-first, bringing together security and diplomatic intelligence that used to be scattered across many agencies. It has about seven hundred thirty staff, and it supports a new council led by the prime minister that met for the first time the same day. Thanks for listening, and see you tomorrow.

73
00:12:44,535 --> 00:12:46,936
[News] また明日。
